        "original_id": "cdf3fe15-775f-58e7-b027-600d999c5cf8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jonny Greenwood, Stanley Donwood, John Leckie, Nigel Godrich\n- Organizations: Radiohead, Trojan Records, Parlophone Records, Capitol Records\n- Products: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller, The Bends, Planet Telex, The Stone Roses\n- Places: Battery Studios, London\n\nFacts:\n- The Bends is the second studio album by Radiohead, and it was released on 13 March 1995 by Parlophone Records in the United Kingdom and by Capitol Records in the United States.\n- The Bends was produced by John Leckie and engineered by Nigel Godrich, who later co-produced all future Radiohead albums.\n- Planet Telex is a song written by Radiohead, and it is the opening track of the 1995 album The Bends.\n- Stanley Donwood has provided artwork for every Radiohead album since The Bends.\n- The group behind The Stone Roses recorded most of that album at Battery Studios in London with producer John Leckie.\n- Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller is a compilation album created by Jonny Greenwood of Radiohead and released on Trojan Records.\n- Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller features artwork by Stanley Donwood.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6ebe615b-6a16-5247-9fcc-56b9d440dab1",
        "text": "Page: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller. Sentence: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller is a compilation album created by Jonny Greenwood of Radiohead and released on Trojan Records.\nPage: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller. Sentence: The album features artwork by Stanley Donwood, who has provided art for every Radiohead album since \"The Bends\" (1995).\nPage: The Bends. Sentence: The Bends (stylised as the bends) is the second studio album by the English alternative rock band Radiohead, released on 13 March 1995 by Parlophone Records in the United Kingdom and by Capitol Records in the United States.\nPage: The Bends. Sentence: The album was produced by John Leckie and engineered by Nigel Godrich, who would go on to co-produce all future albums by the band.\nPage: Planet Telex. Sentence: \"Planet Telex\" is a song written by Radiohead and is the opening track of their 1995 album \"The Bends\".\nPage: The Stone Roses (album). Sentence: The group recorded most of the album at Battery Studios in London with producer John Leckie.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
